{info:title=Kubernetes Vault Integration}
Complete guide for integrating HashiCorp Vault with Kubernetes using native authentication and the Vault Secrets Operator for secure secret management.
{info}

{panel:title=Page Information|borderStyle=dashed|borderColor=#ccc|titleBGColor=#d9ead3|bgColor=#f9f9f9}
*Target Audience:* Kubernetes Engineers, Platform Engineers, DevOps Teams
*Prerequisites:* Kubernetes cluster admin access, Vault cluster access
*Related Pages:* [Keystore Management|03-keystore-management-guide], [Multi-Team Onboarding|08-multi-team-onboarding]
{panel}

h1. Overview

Kubernetes-Vault integration enables secure, dynamic secret management for containerized applications using native Kubernetes authentication and the Vault Secrets Operator.

{panel:title=Integration Benefits|borderStyle=solid|borderColor=#2980b9|titleBGColor=#3498db|titleColor=#ffffff}
• Native Kubernetes authentication with service accounts
• Dynamic secret injection without code changes
• Automatic secret rotation and renewal
• Fine-grained access control per namespace
• Complete audit trail of secret access
{panel}

h1. Architecture

{panel:title=Integration Components|borderStyle=solid|borderColor=#8e44ad|titleBGColor=#9b59b6|titleColor=#ffffff}
*Vault Secrets Operator:* Kubernetes-native secret management
*Kubernetes Auth Method:* Service account-based authentication
*Custom Resources:* VaultAuth, VaultStaticSecret, VaultDynamicSecret
*Service Accounts:* Workload identity for Vault authentication
{panel}

h1. Prerequisites

h2. Kubernetes Requirements

{code:language=bash|title=Verify Kubernetes Prerequisites}
# Check Kubernetes version (1.19+)
kubectl version --short

# Verify cluster admin access
kubectl auth can-i '*' '*' --all-namespaces

# Check for existing Vault Secrets Operator
kubectl get deployment vault-secrets-operator-controller-manager -n vault-secrets-operator-system
{code}

h2. Vault Requirements

{code:language=bash|title=Verify Vault Prerequisites}
# Check Vault connectivity
vault status

# Verify admin permissions
vault auth list
vault secrets list
{code}

h1. Setup

h2. 1. Enable Kubernetes Authentication

{code:language=bash|title=Enable Kubernetes Auth Method}
# Enable Kubernetes auth method
vault auth enable kubernetes

# Get Kubernetes cluster info
K8S_HOST=$(kubectl config view --raw --minify --flatten -o jsonpath='{.clusters[].cluster.server}')
K8S_CA_CERT=$(kubectl config view --raw --minify --flatten -o jsonpath='{.clusters[].cluster.certificate-authority-data}' | base64 -d)

# Create service account for Vault
kubectl create namespace vault-secrets-operator-system
kubectl create serviceaccount vault-auth -n vault-secrets-operator-system

# Create cluster role binding
kubectl create clusterrolebinding vault-auth-delegator \
    --clusterrole=system:auth-delegator \
    --serviceaccount=vault-secrets-operator-system:vault-auth

# Get service account token
REVIEWER_JWT=$(kubectl create token vault-auth -n vault-secrets-operator-system --duration=8760h)

# Configure Kubernetes auth in Vault
vault write auth/kubernetes/config \
    token_reviewer_jwt="$REVIEWER_JWT" \
    kubernetes_host="$K8S_HOST" \
    kubernetes_ca_cert="$K8S_CA_CERT" \
    issuer="https://kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local"
{code}

h2. 2. Install Vault Secrets Operator

{expand:title=Helm Installation}
{code:language=bash|title=Install via Helm}
# Add HashiCorp Helm repository
helm repo add hashicorp https://helm.releases.hashicorp.com
helm repo update

# Install Vault Secrets Operator
helm install vault-secrets-operator hashicorp/vault-secrets-operator \
    --namespace vault-secrets-operator-system \
    --create-namespace

# Verify installation
kubectl get pods -n vault-secrets-operator-system
kubectl wait --for=condition=available --timeout=300s \
    deployment/vault-secrets-operator-controller-manager \
    -n vault-secrets-operator-system
{code}
{expand}

{expand:title=kubectl Installation}
{code:language=bash|title=Install via kubectl}
# Install CRDs and operator
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hashicorp/vault-secrets-operator/main/config/crd/bases/secrets.hashicorp.com_vaultauths.yaml
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hashicorp/vault-secrets-operator/main/config/crd/bases/secrets.hashicorp.com_vaultconnections.yaml
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hashicorp/vault-secrets-operator/main/config/crd/bases/secrets.hashicorp.com_vaultstaticsecrets.yaml
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hashicorp/vault-secrets-operator/main/config/crd/bases/secrets.hashicorp.com_vaultdynamicsecrets.yaml

# Install operator
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hashicorp/vault-secrets-operator/main/config/manager/manager.yaml
{code}
{expand}

h2. 3. Create Vault Policies and Roles

{code:language=bash|title=Create Vault Policies}
# Create application policy
cat > webapp-policy.hcl << 'EOF'
# Read application secrets
path "secret/data/webapp/*" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# Generate database credentials
path "database/creds/webapp" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}
EOF

vault policy write webapp-policy webapp-policy.hcl

# Create Kubernetes role
vault write auth/kubernetes/role/webapp \
    bound_service_account_names=webapp \
    bound_service_account_namespaces=default \
    policies=webapp-policy \
    ttl=1h \
    max_ttl=4h
{code}

h1. Custom Resources

h2. VaultConnection

{code:language=yaml|title=VaultConnection Resource}
apiVersion: secrets.hashicorp.com/v1beta1
kind: VaultConnection
metadata:
  name: default
  namespace: default
spec:
  # Vault cluster address
  address: "https://vault.example.com:8200"
  
  # Skip TLS verification (not recommended for production)
  skipTLSVerify: false
  
  # Optional: Vault namespace (Enterprise feature)
  # vaultNamespace: "app-team"
  
  # Optional: Custom CA certificate
  # caCertSecretRef: "vault-ca-cert"
{code}

h2. VaultAuth

{code:language=yaml|title=VaultAuth Resource}
apiVersion: secrets.hashicorp.com/v1beta1
kind: VaultAuth
metadata:
  name: webapp-auth
  namespace: default
spec:
  # Reference to VaultConnection
  vaultConnectionRef: default
  
  # Authentication method
  method: kubernetes
  mount: kubernetes
  
  # Kubernetes-specific configuration
  kubernetes:
    role: webapp
    serviceAccount: webapp
    
  # Optional: Custom audiences
  # audiences: ["vault", "custom-audience"]
{code}

h2. VaultStaticSecret

{code:language=yaml|title=VaultStaticSecret for KV Secrets}
apiVersion: secrets.hashicorp.com/v1beta1
kind: VaultStaticSecret
metadata:
  name: webapp-config
  namespace: default
spec:
  # Secret type and path
  type: kv-v2
  mount: secret
  path: webapp/config
  
  # Destination Kubernetes secret
  destination:
    name: webapp-config
    create: true
    
  # Authentication reference
  vaultAuthRef: webapp-auth
  
  # Refresh interval
  refreshAfter: 30s
  
  # Optional: Transform secret data
  # hmacSecretData: true
{code}

h2. VaultDynamicSecret

{code:language=yaml|title=VaultDynamicSecret for Database Credentials}
apiVersion: secrets.hashicorp.com/v1beta1
kind: VaultDynamicSecret
metadata:
  name: webapp-db-creds
  namespace: default
spec:
  # Dynamic secret path
  mount: database
  path: creds/webapp
  
  # Destination Kubernetes secret
  destination:
    name: webapp-db-creds
    create: true
    
  # Authentication reference
  vaultAuthRef: webapp-auth
  
  # Renewal settings
  renewalPercent: 67
  revoke: true
  
  # Optional: Custom TTL
  # allowStaticCreds: false
{code}

h1. Application Integration

h2. Deployment Example

{code:language=yaml|title=Application Deployment with Vault Secrets}
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: webapp
  namespace: default
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: webapp
  namespace: default
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: webapp
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: webapp
    spec:
      serviceAccountName: webapp
      containers:
      - name: webapp
        image: nginx:alpine
        env:
        # Static secrets from VaultStaticSecret
        - name: APP_NAME
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: webapp-config
              key: app_name
        - name: API_KEY
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: webapp-config
              key: api_key
              
        # Dynamic database credentials
        - name: DB_USERNAME
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: webapp-db-creds
              key: username
        - name: DB_PASSWORD
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: webapp-db-creds
              key: password
              
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        
        # Health checks
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /health
            port: 80
          initialDelaySeconds: 30
          periodSeconds: 30
          
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /ready
            port: 80
          initialDelaySeconds: 5
          periodSeconds: 10
{code}

h1. Vault Agent Injector

{panel:title=Alternative: Vault Agent Injector|borderStyle=solid|borderColor=#f39c12|titleBGColor=#e67e22|titleColor=#ffffff}
The Vault Agent Injector provides an alternative approach using pod annotations for secret injection via init containers or sidecars.
{panel}

h2. Agent Injector Setup

{code:language=bash|title=Install Vault Agent Injector}
# Install Vault Helm chart with injector
helm repo add hashicorp https://helm.releases.hashicorp.com
helm install vault hashicorp/vault \
    --set "injector.enabled=true" \
    --set "server.enabled=false"
{code}

h2. Pod Annotations

{code:language=yaml|title=Pod with Vault Agent Annotations}
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: webapp
  annotations:
    # Enable Vault Agent injection
    vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject: "true"
    vault.hashicorp.com/role: "webapp"
    
    # Inject database secret
    vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject-secret-database: "secret/webapp/database"
    vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject-template-database: |
      {{- with secret "secret/webapp/database" -}}
      export DB_HOST="{{ .Data.data.host }}"
      export DB_USER="{{ .Data.data.username }}"
      export DB_PASS="{{ .Data.data.password }}"
      {{- end }}
      
    # Inject API keys
    vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject-secret-apikeys: "secret/webapp/apikeys"
    vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject-template-apikeys: |
      {{- with secret "secret/webapp/apikeys" -}}
      export API_KEY="{{ .Data.data.api_key }}"
      export SECRET_KEY="{{ .Data.data.secret_key }}"
      {{- end }}
spec:
  serviceAccountName: webapp
  containers:
  - name: webapp
    image: alpine:latest
    command: ["/bin/sh"]
    args:
    - -c
    - |
      # Source injected secrets
      source /vault/secrets/database
      source /vault/secrets/apikeys
      
      # Start application
      echo "Starting webapp with secrets loaded"
      sleep 3600
{code}

h1. Monitoring and Troubleshooting

h2. Check Resource Status

{code:language=bash|title=Monitor Vault Resources}
# Check VaultConnection status
kubectl get vaultconnection -A
kubectl describe vaultconnection default -n default

# Check VaultAuth status
kubectl get vaultauth -A
kubectl describe vaultauth webapp-auth -n default

# Check VaultStaticSecret status
kubectl get vaultstaticsecret -A
kubectl describe vaultstaticsecret webapp-config -n default

# Check generated Kubernetes secrets
kubectl get secrets -A | grep vault
kubectl describe secret webapp-config -n default
{code}

h2. Operator Logs

{code:language=bash|title=Check Operator Logs}
# View operator logs
kubectl logs -f deployment/vault-secrets-operator-controller-manager \
    -n vault-secrets-operator-system

# Check for specific errors
kubectl logs deployment/vault-secrets-operator-controller-manager \
    -n vault-secrets-operator-system | grep -i error
{code}

h2. Common Issues

{expand:title=Authentication Failures}
*Symptoms:* VaultAuth resources show authentication errors

*Solutions:*
1. Verify service account exists: {{kubectl get sa webapp -n default}}
2. Check Kubernetes role configuration: {{vault read auth/kubernetes/role/webapp}}
3. Verify token reviewer JWT: {{kubectl create token vault-auth -n vault-secrets-operator-system}}
4. Test authentication manually: {{vault write auth/kubernetes/login role=webapp jwt=<token>}}
{expand}

{expand:title=Secret Sync Failures}
*Symptoms:* Kubernetes secrets not created or outdated

*Solutions:*
1. Check VaultStaticSecret status: {{kubectl describe vaultstaticsecret webapp-config}}
2. Verify Vault secret exists: {{vault kv get secret/webapp/config}}
3. Check operator permissions: {{kubectl get clusterrole vault-secrets-operator}}
4. Review operator logs for specific errors
{expand}

h1. Best Practices

{panel:title=Security & Operations|borderStyle=solid|borderColor=#27ae60|titleBGColor=#2ecc71|titleColor=#ffffff}
*Security:*
• Use separate service accounts per application
• Implement least privilege with Vault policies
• Enable audit logging for both Vault and Kubernetes
• Use network policies for namespace isolation

*Operations:*
• Monitor secret sync status and failures
• Set appropriate refresh intervals for secrets
• Implement backup for Vault configuration
• Use GitOps for managing Vault resources
{panel}

